  "id": "lifeline",
  "term": "lifeline",
  "definition": "In this context, a lifeline is a continuous visual profile used in the DIDCO framework to organize and display several parts of a psychiatric work-capacity evaluation together. It is meant as a structured communication tool, so that smooth patterns suggest coherence across domains while breaks or mismatches may point to areas needing closer clinical review.",
